en ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"First"},{"text":"‘s ⊗ keeps strict order on both sides: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a < b"},{"text":" gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a ⊗ c < b ⊗ c"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"c ⊗ a < c ⊗ b"},{"text":" for every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"c"},{"text":" other than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"text":". Integer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TropicalSemiring"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaxPlusSemiring"},{"text":" values keep it (floating point up to rounding), so the lexicographic product","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of either with any selective semiring is a selective semiring, and Dijkstra’s algorithm,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Bellman–Ford and the other selective entry points give best pairs. A bottleneck or Boolean","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first"},{"text":" does not keep it: a narrow edge can tie two paths of different widths, and ⊕ then no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"longer distributes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Shortest paths, the fewest edges among equals.","graph.dijkstraShortestPaths(from: s) { LexicographicSemiring(TropicalSemiring(length[$0]), TropicalSemiring(1)) }"],"syntax":null}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/LexicographicSemiring","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/LexicographicSemiring\/_(_:_:)"],"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/LexicographicSemiring\/init(_:_:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"